{
  "presses": [
    "L-pinky-top",
    "L-index-home",
    "R-pinky-top",
    "R-index-home"
  ],
  "note": "T2: presses [R-index-home,L-ring-bottom,R-index-bottom-in,L-pinky-top] -> {I,O,Q,Z}; rot after {R-middle-top,R-ring-home,R-ring-top}. From T1: L-pinky-top ∩{E,J,Q,Z} -> {Q,Z}. Also L-index-home ∈{E,J,Q,Z}, R-pinky-top ∈{E,J,Q,Z}. Plan T4 press [L-pinky-top,L-index-home,R-pinky-top,R-index-home] to identify which of {Q,Z} is on L-pinky-top."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-index-bottom-in", "L-index-home", "R-index-home"],
  "note": "T4 chord=[L-pinky-top,L-index-bottom-in,L-index-home,R-index-home]. From T3: pre-rot L-pinky-top=Z (got {E,J,O,Z} on [L-pinky-top,L-index-home,R-pinky-top,R-index-home]); post-rot keys {L-index-bottom-in,L-pinky-top,R-middle-top} permuted and L-pinky-top is now !=Z, so Z must be on L-index-bottom-in or R-middle-top. In T4, presence of Z in output => L-index-bottom-in has Z; absence => R-middle-top has Z."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-middle-top", "L-pinky-top", "L-index-home", "R-index-home"],
  "locks": {
    "R-middle-top": "Z"
  },
  "note": "Known: R-middle-top=Z (T4 chord [L-pinky-top,L-index-bottom-in,L-index-home,R-index-home] gave {E,H,O,S} so Z not on L-index-bottom-in; hence Z on R-middle-top). Thus L-index-bottom-in≠Z. Let A=L-pinky-top,B=L-index-bottom-in,C=L-index-home,D=R-index-home. From T4: {A,B,C,D}={E,H,O,S}. T5 chord: {Z,A,C,D} -> set S1={Z,a,c,d}. Next T6: {Z,B,C,D} -> S2={Z,b,c,d}. Then A=S1\\(S1∩S2), B=S2\\(S1∩S2), {C,D}=S1∩S2."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-middle-top", "L-pinky-top", "L-index-bottom-in", "L-index-home"],
  "note": "t7 pressed Z(=R-middle-top),A(L-pinky-top),B(L-index-bottom-in),D(R-index-home)->{H,O,S,Z}. Since in t6 key Z held letter Z and no rotations touched these keys, we get B=S, Z(letter)=Z, and {A,D}={H,O}. From t6 {A,C,D}={E,H,O} => C(letter)=E. Next (t8) press {Z,A,B,C}={R-middle-top,L-pinky-top,L-index-bottom-in,L-index-home}; observe set: if includes H then A=H else A=O (D other)."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-index-bottom", "R-middle-top", "L-pinky-top", "R-index-home"],
  "note": "t10: since no rot, keep R-middle-top=Z (from t9) and L-index-bottom-in=E (from t9). Thus remaining {L-index-bottom,L-middle-top}={B,C}. Plan t11 press {L-index-bottom,R-middle-top(Z),L-pinky-top(H),R-index-home(O)} to identify exact letter on L-index-bottom, then next turn do analogous for L-middle-top."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-ring-home", "R-index-home", "L-pinky-bottom"],
  "note": "Last obs => L-pinky-home=W (keys L-pinky-top=H, R-index-home=O, L-ring-home=R, so 4th=W). Known: L-pinky-top=H; L-pinky-home=W; L-ring-home=R; L-ring-top=N; L-index-bottom=C; L-middle-top=B; R-index-home=O; R-middle-top=Z. Next: press L-pinky-top(H)+L-ring-home(R)+R-index-home(O)+L-pinky-bottom => infer L-pinky-bottom symbol (watch rotation)."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-pinky-top", "L-ring-home", "R-middle-top", "L-index-home"],
  "note": "turn15: no rot => L-pinky-bottom=X. Known: L-pinky-top=H, L-pinky-home=W, L-pinky-bottom=X, L-ring-home=R, L-ring-top=N, L-index-bottom=C, L-middle-top=B, R-index-home=O, R-middle-top=Z. Next press L-pinky-top+L-ring-home+R-middle-top+L-index-home to deduce L-index-home (watch rot)."
}

{
  "presses": ["L-middle-bottom", "L-pinky-top", "R-middle-top", "R-index-home"],
  "note": "Known (as of T17, no rot): L-pinky-top=H,L-pinky-home=W,L-pinky-bottom=X,L-ring-top=N,L-ring-home=R,L-index-top=V,L-index-home=S,L-index-bottom=C,L-middle-top=B,R-index-home=O,R-middle-top=Z. Plan T18 press {L-middle-bottom, L-pinky-top(H), R-middle-top(Z), R-index-home(O)} => if no rot, L-middle-bottom = remaining letter."
}

{
  "presses": ["R-index-top-in", "R-index-home-in", "R-index-bottom-in", "R-middle-top"],
  "note": "Known(no-rot so far): L-ring-top=N, L-ring-home=R, L-middle-top=B, L-ring-bottom=Q. Next after T19 reply: assign observed letters (sorted->keys) to [R-index-top-in,R-index-home-in,R-index-bottom-in,R-middle-top] if rotation notice says none of these 4 rotated; else mark those 4 uncertain. T20 plan: press R-index-top,R-index-home,R-index-bottom,R-ring-top (4 new keys); use set↔keys if no rot among them."
}
